{
	id: "2E008F0FCAA90229"
	group: "499A93482811AC21"
	order_index: 8
	filename: "you_and_what_army"
	title: "You and What Army?"
	subtitle: ["MOD : Minecolonies"]
	default_quest_shape: ""
	default_hide_dependency_lines: false
	quests: [
		{
			title: "Power to the Power User"
			x: -7.5d
			y: 1.5d
			shape: "square"
			subtitle: "MOD : MineColonies"
			description: [
				"&7Hey Bandit, I have an idea..."
				""
				"&7What if we started to band together some of the scattered Power Users, like yourself, into a group?"
				""
				"&7You all are stuck in that world, trying to survive by the FOP Rules. How about we break them in yet another way?"
				""
				"&7See, the FOP Game Server used to have a lot of other systems in it, ones that have been disabled and ripped out, or at least parts of them ripped out. Sometimes something is just so built into the code that isn't possible."
				""
				"&7One of those systems was a Colony system. Instead of building a factory like they want you to, you would build a village, a town, etc. And everyone would work together on things."
				""
				"&7They left most of the code in, I guess to build a Guild system eventually. If you send me, uh... about 20 Vuln Tokens, I think I can reactivate it..."
			]
			dependencies: ["1D0853ADC7295AEB"]
			id: "1EC826482D468EC0"
			tasks: [{
				id: "38A253FB78272BF5"
				type: "item"
				title: "Any 20 Vulnerability Tokens"
				item: {
					id: "itemfilters:tag"
					Count: 1b
					tag: {
						value: "tfb2:tfb2_vulnerability"
					}
				}
				count: 20L
				consume_items: true
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "784FBAC4F3426FAD"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Ready your Caravan!"
			x: -7.5d
			y: 0.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Aha, yes yes! Okay, Bandit, get ready, cause it's time to make an army. Or more accurately, it's time to start your own branch of the Ferret Business!"
				""
				"&7Send me Silver Coins so I can get some Power User's attention. Meanwhile, you'll want this Supply Camp summoner."
				""
				"&7Where should you build it? Probably the edge of a hex to start, with all the surrounding hexes being land. At least that's my suggestion, you can expand a good amount."
				""
				"&7When you have a location, Right Click the Supply Camp onto the center of where you want to deploy it.  You'll get a ghost outline showing you where it'll build. They have a lot of built in camp styles, cycle them with the arrows in the upper right."
				""
				"&7The system will tell you what to fix if you try to build it and it has a problem. Just fix what it shows, then try deploying again."
			]
			dependencies: ["1EC826482D468EC0"]
			id: "549729CAC679BFA8"
			tasks: [{
				id: "659A885E8642F38C"
				type: "item"
				item: "calemiutils:coin_penny"
				count: 50L
				consume_items: true
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "410876FF99AB4409"
				type: "item"
				item: "minecolonies:supplycampdeployer"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "This is YOUR Town!"
			x: -6.25d
			y: 0.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Okay, I mentioned you should build your Supply Camp on the edge of a hex, right? That's because you also need to put up a Town Hall!"
				""
				"&7Explore your camp. Look in all the chests and barrels, you might find some extra supplies. You'll also find a Town Hall spawner, and a Build Tool. That second thing you especially want for building your Colony!"
				""
				"&7This Town Hall is best built in the center of a Hex! Be sure to check out my warning info branching off the last quest, please. It's important to know!"
				""
				"&7Using the Build Tool, you can change the building and style with the arrows and drop downs along the top! Some have lots of different styles, they had a lot of options in this they never used again."
				""
				"&7Oh yeah, if you can't find the Town Hall or Build Tool, you can just craft em."
			]
			dependencies: ["549729CAC679BFA8"]
			id: "5E850496FA415E4D"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "57E8FACD81160263"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhuttownhall"
				}
				{
					id: "68B74FB2136A9592"
					type: "item"
					item: "structurize:sceptergold"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "3893D4819F2FC250"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			icon: {
				id: "botania:cosmetic_questgiver_mark"
				Count: 1b
				tag: { }
			}
			x: -7.5d
			y: -0.75d
			shape: "gear"
			description: [
				"&7Hey Bandit, real real quick this is important."
				""
				"&7If you have other Assistants with you, and you all want to run your own Business, this is important!"
				""
				"&7After you place the Supply Camp, you'll need to place down a Town Hall to start getting Power Users together."
				""
				"&7THE PLACE YOU PUT THE TOWN HALL IS IMPORTANT!"
				""
				"&7The Colony system marks the 4 chunks in every direction of the Town Hall as part of YOUR town. That's 64 blocks in every direction. If your Town Hall is the center of a Hex, you're town will cover most of the six surrounding hexes!"
				""
				"&7Be sure you and the other Assistants spread out your towns! This'll be good, since when your town is large enough, you can jump between town halls!"
			]
			dependencies: ["549729CAC679BFA8"]
			dependency_requirement: "one_started"
			size: 0.75d
			id: "4C99DBD766F8F27B"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5BC715D99F89F00C"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "MINE COLONY NOTES"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Time to Build"
			x: -5.0d
			y: 0.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7What, you set out the town hall, selected a style, but it didn't build? It just marked out an area? One moment..."
				""
				"&7Oh, of course. Only the Supply Camp has 'free resources'. Everything else in the Colony system requires you to collect the resources yourself. "
				""
				"&7You'll also notice that no Power Users have shown up yet. You need to find the center Town Hall podium and Right Click it, then select Create New Colony."
				""
				"&7Your friendly Power Users (or should we call them Citizens?) will show up shortly. But be warned : the hostile life around you is hostile to them too! They'll be showing up with minimal equipment, so that the FOP doesn't get alerted to this."
				""
				"&7Be prepared to defend your Citizens while you start building your Colony."
			]
			dependencies: ["5E850496FA415E4D"]
			id: "57E22E4331DA642C"
			tasks: [{
				id: "028FB99D18C3D2FC"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Building for the Builder"
			x: -5.0d
			y: -1.0d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Before your Town Hall can be built, you need a place for the Builder citizen to set up shop. Craft yourself a Builder's Hut and place it out like you did the Town Hall and Supply Camp!"
				""
				"&7It'll set out a roped off area and a 'control' block for it, usually a desk. Right Click it, and you can see a lot of info on the building, like which Citizen is assigned to it, and what resources it needs so it can be built."
				""
				"&7The Red ? mark in the lower left has a lot of useful tips I got added to the system. Be sure to check them."
				""
				"&7Now you can click the Build Options button, and cycle through the styles to make sure you can get the resources for the building. Be sure to check your stocks and the area for enough!"
				""
				"&7Then you just need to select a style, and hit Build Building! Then just start adding resources the Builder wants, until it is done."
			]
			dependencies: ["57E22E4331DA642C"]
			id: "65C762C37D2F5310"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3C864C92E59E86A9"
				type: "item"
				item: "minecolonies:blockhutbuilder"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "2D5565353B525123"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Busy Builders"
			x: -3.75d
			y: -1.0d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Oh. Notice how there's a red icon above the Builder's head? That means they are missing something for the next step. As you are just starting out, well...that means what is missing is most likely a Shovel or a Pickaxe."
				""
				"&7Right Click the Builder and they'll tell you what they want, and show an example. For your new Builder Hut, they can only use Wood or Gold tools."
				""
				"&7Since Gold doesn't grow on trees (usually), make a Wooden Shovel for them. The you can either Right Click the builder and get into their Inventory and drop the Shovel into it. Or, you can drop it into the Builder Hut table and either wait or hit the Request Pickup button."
				""
				"&7They are going to ask for a LOT of items to start with... don't worry, this'll become a good Colony soon enough, Bandit!"
			]
			dependencies: ["65C762C37D2F5310"]
			id: "01BAE55B6B3047E1"
			tasks: [{
				id: "78BB66BCACDE0F28"
				type: "item"
				item: {
					id: "minecraft:wooden_shovel"
					Count: 1b
					tag: {
						Damage: 0
					}
				}
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "2419CD38128E5AAB"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Restful Spot"
			x: -3.75d
			y: -2.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Well, Bandit, you could get that Town Hall built up now if you want, but personally? I suggest getting the Tavern up and running."
				""
				"&7Mostly because it gives your Citizens a place to rest at night, instead of hovering at the Town Hall table all night."
				""
				"&7It will also entice other Power Users to stop by that you can recruit to your Colony, though you'll need to have Houses for everyone first."
				""
				"&7Oh, I also suggest upgrading your Builder Hut to level 2 at least, so that they can use better tools. And work faster."
				""
				"&7And... a guard tower would probably REALLY help. You could hire NPC Mercenaries but... by design, they steal from your Citizens? What the hell, I can't disable it. Eh whatever, you can risk it if you want."
			]
			dependencies: ["01BAE55B6B3047E1"]
			id: "0DA2CC16D8348BFD"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7983685919D2CF25"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhuttavern"
				}
				{
					id: "664CB754E621A1AC"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhutguardtower"
				}
			]
		}
		{
			title: "Housed and Fed"
			x: -0.5d
			y: -2.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7So, a guard tower, a tavern, what else do...oh, duh. I already mentioned it, but you need to build some houses for your current Citizens if you want to expand your Colony. Each floor of a house fits one person, so you'll need to either build lots of level 1 houses, or start upgrading them and your Builder Huts."
				""
				"&7You'll also want to build a Restaurant. You could just make food yourself and give it to each Citizen, but its easier if you have a Restaurant."
				""
				"&7The restaurant can be taught how to make any food recipe you know, and you can tell it what fuel it is allowed to use to cook food."
			]
			dependencies: ["0DA2CC16D8348BFD"]
			id: "0660E08D755B3BB6"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "1C693B31EC428617"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhutcitizen"
				}
				{
					id: "7A4CF4EF10673BEC"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhutcook"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "039330EEE79922C8"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Keeping Stocks"
			x: -3.75d
			y: -3.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7As you expand your Colony, you're going to run yourself ragged if you try to keep your builders, your guards, and everyone supplied, fed, and healthy all on your own."
				""
				"&7For sure, you'll want to build a Warehouse and a Courier."
				""
				"&7The Warehouse has a lot of Racks to store items in (Don't try to add any yourself, the Colony system won't recognize them, unfortunately). Each level you upgrade it adds even more storage space."
				""
				"&7But to get the stored items to the Builders, Cooks, etc who need them, you'll need to build and hire a Courier as well."
				""
				"&7A Courier will run around, taking unneeded items from buildings and storing them, and transporting needed items from the Warehouse. Improving your Courier lets them carry more each trip."
			]
			dependencies: ["0DA2CC16D8348BFD"]
			id: "182125537D52D5CB"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "4A0ABFA45A2854BF"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhutwarehouse"
				}
				{
					id: "02AA286F2B5B2C74"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhutdeliveryman"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "20608CE875773AF8"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Requests!"
			x: -3.75d
			y: 0.0d
			shape: "gear"
			description: [
				"&7So you'll notice a second icon above your Citizen's heads, an orange speech bubble. This means they want something less critically, but still important. "
				""
				"&7For requests like Tools, your Citizens have a small range of acceptable tools, depending on their level and the level of their workplace."
				""
				"&7A level 1 Builder Hut only uses wood or gold, while a Level 2 uses stone, etc."
				""
				"&7In the Citizens information page, you can get a closer look at their requests in the Requests tab at the left. If there's a certain type of tool they want, they'll mention it, such as needing an Iron Pickaxe, or a Shovel thats either Wood or Stone."
			]
			dependencies: ["01BAE55B6B3047E1"]
			size: 0.75d
			id: "7A962D53F27D9F6F"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3D02C0323861682E"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Always At Paw"
			x: -4.75d
			y: -3.5d
			shape: "gear"
			description: [
				"&7Work buildings like the Builder Hut, Restaurant, and others have a tab called Minimum Stock. This is very useful for Couriers."
				""
				"&7Unneeded items at Colony buildings will be moved to the Warehouse if you have a Courier. But setting a Minimum Stock of items a building uses regularly is a good idea for a few reasons : "
				"&7  1) Less trips, for both the Worker and the Courier. "
				"  &72) Better use of space: As you grow, the warehouse will fill quickly. Keeping items stored at the buildings that use them is a good idea."
			]
			dependencies: ["182125537D52D5CB"]
			size: 0.75d
			id: "6207A71B005AEA31"
			tasks: [{
				id: "266C61FB8C0A83AC"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Life and Death"
			x: -4.6875d
			y: -2.25d
			shape: "gear"
			description: [
				"&7The FOP Game Server is super dangerous, Bandit. For you, but especially your Citizens!"
				""
				"&7If you haven't yet, you'll probably have a Citizen die at some point. They'll create a Grave with all their items, but this won't last forever."
				""
				"&7But if these are Power Users that can respawn, why don't they just respawn in the Colony?"
				""
				"&7Well, to activate and get the Colony system working again, I needed to make some adjustments. When a Power User joins your colony, they leave behind their stuff so they don't trip the FOP Security Systems."
				""
				"&7And when they \"die\" as one of your Citizens, they return to their Power User life, so someone else can come in. Otherwise, we run the risk of alerting the FOP to this system being used as a way to exploit the system."
			]
			dependencies: ["0DA2CC16D8348BFD"]
			size: 0.75d
			id: "370F8492AAA1A477"
			tasks: [{
				id: "309F2F0558E6121F"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Happy Homes"
			x: -1.3125d
			y: -1.3125d
			shape: "gear"
			description: [
				"&7You know that whole Project MMO gear restriction system? The one Kowa mostly tapped down? Well, it's mostly only tapped down for YOU, not other Power Users."
				""
				"&7This is really obvious within the Colony system. Your Citizens cannot use a lot of more powerful items right off the bat. Heck, they are limited to WOOD tools at the start!"
				""
				"&7But they can quickly start using better tools if you raise the level of their Work AND themselves!"
				""
				"&7Upgrading buildings is simple, just select Upgrade in the Building Options menu for the building, and let the Builder do the Build thing."
				""
				"&7But Citizens can get stronger and better stats as they work, and they too level up, but only if their work AND their Home is higher level as well!"
			]
			dependencies: ["0660E08D755B3BB6"]
			size: 0.75d
			id: "7DBB22AA6A8B133B"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AC8A29305F4DC9C"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Growing Colony"
			x: 2.5d
			y: -2.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7With a growing colony, and a restaurant, you probably have a growing request for food. And stocking your Restaurant yourself is a bit time consuming, yeah?"
				""
				"&7So, how about getting your Citizens to grow their own meals? By building a Farm I mean, they can grow a lot of different foods for themselves."
				""
				"&7Along with the Farm is the Field, basically a scarecrow that denotes the center of a Field. The building itself usually places one for you, but every level the Farm is at, is another field. Two levels, two fields, etc"
				""
				"&7You can tell a farmer what crop a field should be by placing the seed for the crop in the Scarecrow. For things like Potatoes, just put the potato there. Simple!"
				""
				"&7You can also teach the Farmer how to craft things like Hay Bales, seeds, etc."
			]
			dependencies: ["0660E08D755B3BB6"]
			id: "2235E571003AAC12"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "3B6DE8FD21C1D7FE"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhutfarmer"
				}
				{
					id: "6B69DA9CEEC1F8A9"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhutfield"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "491950B119FBD716"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Supply the Supply"
			x: -3.75d
			y: -4.75d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7You have a place to store resources and materials, now you should probably get your Citizens gathering some of the basics for you."
				""
				"&7The Forester's Hut will chop trees down around it, gathering the Wood, Saplings, and other things the trees may provide. If there is a tree you don't want chopped down, put a Cobblestone under the trunk."
				""
				"&7You can set what trees the Forester will chop down in the interface, as well as setting whether they'll replant trees, or keep to a specific area. To set the area, hit Get Tool and Right Click the two corners of the area."
				""
				"&7The Mine will dig downward, gathering stone, ores, and more it finds. The first level of the Mine will make mineshafts at Y 50, 2 at Y30, then 3 and higher at Bedrock. "
				""
				"&7You'll need to level up the Mine to get the rarer ores, and the Miner might be very picky on pickaxes. The system is slightly messed up, the FOP never fixed it for the new materials they found."
			]
			dependencies: ["182125537D52D5CB"]
			id: "21B9FFB35339D0A3"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "633E69858187DA83"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhutlumberjack"
				}
				{
					id: "4FAA45E5F645CB6C"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhutminer"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "620E4DA12A8B0656"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Flying Friends"
			x: 1.25d
			y: -3.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7You can make Farms that take care of Chickens and Bees specifically."
				""
				"&7For a Chicken Farmer's Hut, you'll need to bring them two chickens to start out. Youc an also set if they'll breed and slaughter chickens, and if they'll collect eggs."
				""
				"&7For the Apiary, it may not be as useful. The Colony system only knows how to handle normal Bees, and vanilla Apiary's it needs to take care of them. Our special Resourceful Bees don't work well in them."
			]
			dependencies: ["2235E571003AAC12"]
			id: "3177F4BC0D9887AA"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "363202AB3B78A970"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhutchickenherder"
				}
				{
					id: "7298FF96FE95E6C3"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhutbeekeeper"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "0B2A02F316503D01"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Farm Hands"
			x: 0.0d
			y: -3.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Farms are more than just growing crops, you can also raise Sheep, Cows, Pigs, and Rabbits."
				""
				"&7Each of these animals requires a specific Hut or Hutch. You will also have to supply two of the animals to get them started."
				""
				"&7Each building has settings you can change to tell them whether they should breed and slaughter animals, collect things like milk from cows, etc."
				""
				"&7Appropriate food will be needed for the animals as well."
			]
			dependencies: ["2235E571003AAC12"]
			id: "594A8CBEB1DC7697"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "0EF92AE164EB3E4F"
					type: "item"
					item: "minecolonies:blockhutcowboy"
				}
				{
					id: "2D6AD25A5E08C6F7"
					type: "item"
